## README.md

### Color Palette Picker – Tkinter App

**What it does:**  
This desktop application helps you build and manage small custom color palettes (up to five colors). You can select each color visually using the built-in picker dialog; the chosen colors are displayed live on the interface both as colored boxes (swatches) and their hexadecimal codes.

You can easily copy any hex code by clicking "Copy," or export your current palette to a `.txt` file via "Save Palette".

**How it works:**

- **Pick Colors:** Click "Pick" next to each slot; choose from the pop-up dialog.
- **View Swatches:** Each selected slot shows its actual shade and hex value.
- **Copy Hex Code:** Click "Copy" beside any filled slot—its value goes straight into your clipboard.
- **Save Your Work:** Use "Save Palette" at the bottom—choose where you want your `.txt` list of selected hex values saved.

The interface uses modern dark tones (`#23272f`, `#2c313a`) with clean Segoe UI fonts for clarity and professionalism. All controls are spaced for usability.

**Requirements:**
Python 3.x (Tkinter comes standard).

Run by saving `palette_picker.py` then:

```bash
python palette_picker.py
```

Enjoy building beautiful palettes!